            "verb": "insert-piece"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-hang-a-tile",
        "note": "A fourth tile is hung off the tail's spare socket. The `prefab` on the verb is a DRIFT GUARD: it names what the solve must have put at that index, so a re-solve that moves a tile reds instead of editing the wrong one."
      },
      {
        "area": "area/annex",
        "edits": [
          {
            "piece": 3,
            "prefab": "prefab/gallery-annex-cell",
            "verb": "swap-piece",
            "with": "prefab/gallery-annex-end"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-cap-the-tail",
        "note": "The new tail becomes the terminal tile. A swap needs a replacement that can present a connector at every socket the old piece had mated, which is why it is the TAIL that can change and not a middle tile."
      },
      {
        "area": "area/annex",
        "edits": [
          {
            "piece": 3,
            "prefab": "prefab/gallery-annex-end",
            "verb": "remove-piece"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-take-it-off",
        "note": "And it comes off again. Removals come BEFORE rewires in an area's script — removing shifts the indices every later rewire is written against."
      },
      {
        "area": "area/annex",
        "edits": [
          {
            "piece": 1,
            "prefab": "prefab/gallery-annex-cell",
            "verb": "reseed-piece"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-reroll-the-middle",
        "note": "The middle tile is re-rolled against the pool. After the removal, so it cannot move a tile out from under an earlier verb's index, and before the two rewires, which act on the join it re-mates."
      },
      {
        "area": "area/annex",
        "edits": [
          {
            "piece": 0,
            "prefab": "prefab/gallery-annex-entry",
            "socket": 0,
            "state": "sealed",
            "verb": "rewire-socket"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-seal-a-way",
        "note": "A mated socket is sealed shut — the other half of the socket vocabulary."
      },
      {
        "area": "area/annex",
        "edits": [
          {
            "piece": 0,
            "prefab": "prefab/gallery-annex-entry",
            "socket": 0,
            "state": "open",
            "verb": "rewire-socket"
          }
        ],
        "id": "batch/annex-open-a-way",
        "note": "And the entry's own side of that join is opened again. `rewire-socket open` clears an UNMATED socket's seal, so it can only ever be written on a socket with nothing mated to it — and the cell one step past such an opening lies outside every placed tile. In a world with nothing outside, that is a bottomless column, and `DW0322` refuses the doorway: a way out onto nothing is a fall nobody survives. The one unmated socket that does NOT face the void is the one the batch above just severed, because the partner's own plane is still walled. So this opens the near side of a bricked-up doorway and leaves the far side brick — which is what the verb draws, and it is laid last because the socket is mated until then."
      },
